```markdown:GitHub Pages Setup Guide:github-guide.md
# Next Steps to Get Your Tracker Online

I noticed in your screenshot that your repository is set to **Private**. To host a webpage for free on GitHub Pages, the repository needs to be **Public**. Here are the exact steps to finish getting your app online:

### 1. Upload Your File

1. After clicking "uploading an existing file", drag and drop your HTML tracker file into the box on the screen.

2. **Important:** Ensure your file is named exactly `index.html`. If it has a different name (like `tracker.html`), rename it on your computer first before uploading it, otherwise the web hosting won't find it automatically.

3. Scroll down and click the green **Commit changes** button.

### 2. Make Your Repository Public (Required for Free Hosting)

**Privacy Note:** While making the repository public means anyone could technically read your HTML code, **your student data is 100% private and secure**. Because the app requires your Google login and saves data to your personal Firebase database, absolutely no one else can see your students or your tracker data.

1. Click the **Settings** tab (the gear icon) at the top of your repository page.

2. Scroll all the way down to the bottom of the Settings page until you see the red **Danger Zone**.

3. Click **Change repository visibility** and select **Change to public**. Follow the on-screen prompts to confirm.

*(Alternative: If you absolutely must keep the code private, do not use GitHub Pages. Instead, go to [Netlify.com](https://www.netlify.com/), create a free account, and connect it to your private GitHub repository).*

### 3. Turn on GitHub Pages

1. Still in the **Settings** tab, look at the left-hand menu and click **Pages**.

2. Under the "Build and deployment" section, look for the **Branch** dropdown (it will likely say "None").

3. Change "None" to **main** (or **master**) and click **Save**.

### 4. Wait for Your Link!

Wait about 1 to 2 minutes, then refresh that **Pages** screen. You will see a notification at the top saying *"Your site is live at..."* with a web address. Click that link, and your app is officially online!

---

### 5. 🚨 NEW: Connect Your Free Database (Fixes the Endless Loading Spinner)

If your app is stuck on an endless loading spinner, it means it is trying to connect to a database to save your students, but doesn't have the keys yet! Here is how to get a free Firebase database and connect it:

1. **Create a Database:** Go to [console.firebase.google.com](https://console.firebase.google.com/).
2. Click **Create a project**, name it "TISA Tracker" (or anything you want), and click continue until it finishes creating.
3. **Register your Web App:** On the project overview page, click the little **`</>` (Web)** icon in the center of the screen. Name the app "Tracker" and click **Register app**.
4. **Copy the Keys:** Firebase will show you a block of code called `firebaseConfig`. It looks like this:
   ```javascript
   const firebaseConfig = {
     apiKey: "YOUR_API_KEY",
     authDomain: "your-project.firebaseapp.com",
     // ...
   };
   ```
   **Copy the entire block of code.**
5. **Turn on the Database:** Still in Firebase, look at the left-hand menu, click **Build > Firestore Database**, and click **Create Database**. Make sure to select **Start in Test mode** when it asks!
6. **Paste into GitHub:** Go back to your GitHub repository and open your `index.html` file. 
7. Click the **Pencil Icon** to edit the file.
8. Look near the very top of the code (around line 39) for the giant `🚨 YOUR FIREBASE CONFIGURATION GOES HERE 🚨` section.
9. Replace the empty `const myFirebaseConfig = {};` with the code block you copied from Firebase.
10. Click the green **Commit changes...** button. Wait 2 minutes, refresh your site, and the loading spinner will be gone forever!

