### 🚨 Troubleshooting: "File not found" Error

If you click your live link and see a **"File not found"** error, it means GitHub cannot find a file named `index.html`. Here is how to fix it without re-uploading:

1. Go back to your main repository page (click the `<> Code` tab at the top left).
2. Look at the list of files. Find the HTML file you uploaded (e.g., `tracker.html` or `Index.html`).
3. Click on the file name to open it.
4. Click the **pencil icon** (Edit this file) in the top right corner of the file box.
5. At the top left, change the file name so it says exactly **`index.html`** (all lowercase).
6. Click the green **Commit changes...** button at the top right.
7. **Wait about 2 minutes** for GitHub to rebuild your site, then refresh your web address!
